  "SourceElements": [
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-001",
      "SourceSection": "25.1: Notice & Wonder: A Snowflake’s Return",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What do you notice? What do you wonder?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-002",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Earlier, we learned that the \\(n\\)th term of a geometric sequence with an initial value of \\(a\\) and a common ratio of \\(r\\) is \\(a(r^{n-1})\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-003",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For a Koch Snowflake, it turns out that we can find the number of triangles added on at each iteration by having \\(a=3\\) and \\(r=4\\). The sum \\(s\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms in this geometric sequence tell us how many triangles total make…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle s = 3+3(4)+3(4^2)+ . . . +3(4^{n-1})\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "More generally, the sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of any geometric sequence can be expressed as",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle s = a+a(r)+a(r^2)+ . . . +a(r^{n-1})\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle s = a(1+r+r^2+ . . . +r^{n-1})\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What would happen if we multiplied each side of this equation by \\((1-r)\\)? (hint: \\((x-1)(x^3+x^2+x+1)=x^4-1\\).)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Rewrite the new equation in the form of \\(s = \\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Use this new formula to calculate how many triangles after the original are in the first 5, 10, and 15 iterations of the Koch Snowflake.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "25.2: A Geometric Addition Formula",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If the initial triangle has sides that are each one unit long, find an equation for the perimeter \\(P\\) of the Koch Snowflake after the \\(n\\)th iteration and graph \\((n,P)\\) for iterations 0 through 5.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Han is prescribed a course of antibiotics for an infection. He is told to take a 150 mg dose of the antibiotic regularly every 12 hours for 15 days. Han is curious about the antibiotic and learns that at the end of the 12 hours, only 5% of…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "How much of the antibiotic is in the body right after the first, second, and third doses?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "When will the total amount of the antibiotic in Han be highest over the course of the 15 day treatment? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes identities can help us see and write a pattern in a simpler form. Imagine a chessboard where 1 grain of rice is placed on the first square, 2 on the second, 4 on the third, and so on. How many grains of rice are on the 64-square…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle s = 1 + 2 + 4 + . . . + 2^{63}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If we rewrite this expression as \\(2^{63}+ . . . + 2^2 + 2 + 1\\), we have an expression similar to one we’ve seen before, \\(x^{n-1} + x^{n-2} + . . . +x^2+x+1\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In an earlier lesson, we showed that \\((x - 1)(x^{n-1} + x^{n-2} + . . . +x^2+x+1)\\) is equivalent to the simpler expression \\((x^{n} -1)\\). Using this identity with \\(x=2\\) and \\(n=64\\), we have",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle \\begin{align*} (2^{64-1} + 2^{64-2} + . . . +2^2+2+1) &= s \\\\ (2 - 1)(2^{64-1} + 2^{64-2} + . . . +2^2+2+1) &= (2-1)s \\\\ 2^{64}-1 &= (2-1)s \\\\ \\frac{2^{64}-1}{2-1} &= s \\\\ 2^{64}-1 &= s\\\\ \\end{align*}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "This means that the sum total of all the grains of rice is \\(2^{64}-1\\), or \\(18,\\!446,\\!744,\\!073,\\!709,\\!551,\\!615\\). More generally, for any geometric sequence starting at \\(a\\) with a common ratio \\(r\\), the sum \\(s\\) of the first…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L25-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "25.3: The Sum of Antibiotics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "An equation which is true for all values of the variables in it.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l25.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
